#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115056 :question/id #uuid "32bd6b27-e95d-5de4-941f-309eb0bc61f1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4411" :question/problem "Find $AB-CB,$ where\n\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad B=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{3} & -45 \\\\ 81 & -\\sqrt{5} & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAB-CB=(A-C)B.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A-C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-C & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB-CB & =(A-C)B \\\\  & =-{I}_{3}B \\\\  & =-B \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{3} & 45 \\\\ -81 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115057 :question/id #uuid "3b1395b6-49c1-5e0d-ac94-c2d6fc242f6b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4412" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC,$ where\n\n\n$$\nA= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad B= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}, \\quad C= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC = (AB)C = A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3 \\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3 \\times 1$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3 \\times 3$ matrix that will require finding $9$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $3 \\times 1$ matrix that will require finding only $3$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115058 :question/id #uuid "7ab158e6-4222-5cab-88a0-85ce74a7d4b2" :question/math-academy-id "e-4413" :question/problem "Given that $A, B,$ and $C$ are $6 \\times 6$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nI. $A(BC) = (AB)C$\n\nII. $A(B+C) = BA+CA$\n\nIII. $A(B+C) = AB+AC$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C = A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B+C) = AB + AC$ in general. However, since matrix multiplication is not commutative, we have\n\n$$\nAB + AC  \\neq BA + CA.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C = AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C) = AB+AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115828 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "334cfb64-857e-505a-9a43-d21f8e1caef8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 7 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392430} {:answer/id #uuid "aad0983e-16d3-5538-b3b8-9b0e2aff415b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ -15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392431} {:answer/id #uuid "83c87507-4794-5dbb-9918-43c4f3143e69" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392432} {:answer/id #uuid "6010500b-541c-5b97-806c-4f018455b4cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392433} {:answer/id #uuid "5816752b-1281-5b14-8078-9753e15cfdd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 15 \\\\ 3 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5816752b-1281-5b14-8078-9753e15cfdd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 15 \\\\ 3 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392434} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a0ff826-a7be-5da5-888c-b90181819cf0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d05ca169-7c67-546f-9f08-0fce1486794c" :question/math-academy-id "q-41785" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -3 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 15 \\\\ 3 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115829 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9607e1e7-f8ac-53de-9908-c1f571a0116f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{5} & -\\sqrt{6} & -1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{7} & -\\sqrt{2} & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113912} {:answer/id #uuid "a6768771-f5b7-548e-999b-f6902415943b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113913} {:answer/id #uuid "3fb0f0a6-006f-5c75-b1b8-e221a96e83b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113914} {:answer/id #uuid "44d07522-65f1-56fb-9042-731bbe25d2a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{2} & 2\\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{5} & 2\\sqrt{6} & 2 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{7} & 2\\sqrt{2} & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113915} {:answer/id #uuid "7d1284d9-c607-5679-ad2a-4ed9873a1875" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{6} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113916}] :answer-field/id #uuid "80098924-46d2-51df-aebc-a0350ae533b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113911}] :question/id #uuid "9796bb85-e5f6-55ad-ade8-918ae279a8e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42004" :question/problem "Calculate $BA + BC$, where\n$$\n\\displaystyle A = \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{6} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115835 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c24ee771-dbe8-598f-84ff-60f041661edb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113948} {:answer/id #uuid "31f22e55-3257-560c-9b8b-1a370672646f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113949} {:answer/id #uuid "41fb8df9-f182-543a-ad39-bd4d9406f6c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113950} {:answer/id #uuid "4c8e5b8a-9724-51db-b122-6afd0420a1df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113951} {:answer/id #uuid "63361cf3-7b7e-5c0a-8a4d-0ce1232f5d05" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113952}] :answer-field/id #uuid "9e1c3b65-2a4d-5f95-b0da-0c05529f3648" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113947}] :question/id #uuid "7171223c-0a20-5fbc-a656-b17651c3059d" :question/math-academy-id "q-42257" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n$$\n\\displaystyle A = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 5 & -5 & -5\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115836 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13773284-d540-59d5-9332-97c84b837ffe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484855} {:answer/id #uuid "a397a770-fb84-5803-b445-bb962f0edcc9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{2} & -1 & -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -1 & -\\sqrt{5} & -1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{7} & -1 & -\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485172} {:answer/id #uuid "bd233e28-d1ff-5b24-a20c-c4ce4f8e0913" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485224} {:answer/id #uuid "ca909ceb-d495-5fda-9394-cd7bfc79f6cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\sqrt{2} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -2 & -2\\sqrt{5} & -2 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{7} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485248} {:answer/id #uuid "d61c9def-9523-5682-a82f-7beb698de51e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca909ceb-d495-5fda-9394-cd7bfc79f6cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\sqrt{2} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -2 & -2\\sqrt{5} & -2 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{7} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485248} :answer-field/id #uuid "5acf797e-8560-5305-87b5-ad22ffde0a24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "008d2c2b-6bdc-5e16-92ee-368e3b3e4390" :question/math-academy-id "q-42263" :question/problem "Find $AB+CB$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -1 \\\\ -9 & 10 & 11\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 9 & -10 & -13\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAB+CB=(A+C)B.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+C & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -1 \\\\ -9 & 10 & 11\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 9 & -10 & -13\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-2{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB+CB & =(A+C)B \\\\  & =-2{I}_{3}B \\\\  & =-2B \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\sqrt{2} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -2 & -2\\sqrt{5} & -2 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{7} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115837 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1067aa3d-2b51-5b1a-b638-8cd254e921c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448632} {:answer/id #uuid "a3967aa3-4b50-5c5c-b5fe-aa477f5fe032" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1067aa3d-2b51-5b1a-b638-8cd254e921c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448632} :answer-field/id #uuid "149d811f-1bfd-59da-848a-31d1c4100def" :answer-field/key "$AB=BA$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449356} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86075d40-0e3f-586b-9449-798158d86bca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448634} {:answer/id #uuid "1fec6718-135d-53ed-ace0-3373f23e193b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fec6718-135d-53ed-ace0-3373f23e193b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448635} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cdc4938-08ac-5768-9c3a-6cf1b96bf157" :answer-field/key "$(AB)C=A(BC)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449357} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8546691d-f8b4-5754-96f8-903691eb5eb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448636} {:answer/id #uuid "d2f078ae-15b0-55b8-85f1-fb559cdbab88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2f078ae-15b0-55b8-85f1-fb559cdbab88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448637} :answer-field/id #uuid "0bc3e7d1-fdc0-5ebf-9944-36f12a7d8eff" :answer-field/key "$AC+BC=(A+B)C$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449358}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "5e648555-87e2-52bf-ac70-24ae7f7d32c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-42265" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $4\\times 4$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement $AB=BA$ is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement $(AB)C=A(BC)$ is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general.\n\n- Statement $AC+BC=(A+B)C$ is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C=AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C)=AB+AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements $(AB)C=A(BC)$ and $AC+BC=(A+B)C$ are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115838 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84adee91-f9b3-5089-890e-41b5e257813d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448638} {:answer/id #uuid "e2e31c4f-b7bd-5276-a991-deb172fd1702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448639}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2e31c4f-b7bd-5276-a991-deb172fd1702" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448639} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d1bd3d1-8fdb-5689-a908-f1bc0ac9ac01" :answer-field/key "$(A+B)C=AC+BC$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449359} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1670a685-9e94-5937-8cfd-7d0d29af6eb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448640} {:answer/id #uuid "16ec1bf8-e36a-5bfb-84bd-a4334c07e464" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448641}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1670a685-9e94-5937-8cfd-7d0d29af6eb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448640} :answer-field/id #uuid "64b55508-2a98-5d52-9e53-d6536bd357ec" :answer-field/key "$AB=BA$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449360} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "113b4e99-4e5b-55aa-a4da-2a14a868af02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448642} {:answer/id #uuid "056450c3-2bbe-583e-950a-5fcae4730b42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "113b4e99-4e5b-55aa-a4da-2a14a868af02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448642} :answer-field/id #uuid "96d5b3ee-a8ea-534b-8e66-6ca762d54d43" :answer-field/key "$A(BC)=(BA)C$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "174631dd-f119-50e8-bf7b-ac669b330d64" :question/math-academy-id "q-42266" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $6\\times 6$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement $(A+B)C=AC+BC$ is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+B)C=AC+BC,$ and $A(B+C)=AB+AC$ in general.\n\n- Statement $AB=BA$ is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement $A(BC)=(BA)C$ is false. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AB)C=A(BC)$ in general. However, since matrix multiplication is not commutative, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A(BC) &=(AB)C\\ne (BA)C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only statement $(A+B)C=AC+BC$ is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235392 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83e8b5b8-2dc6-502f-9895-61592963799f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "83e8b5b8-2dc6-502f-9895-61592963799f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234745} :answer-field/id #uuid "73f19ed8-00ca-518c-b9b0-9aa8b5d98ca5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235100} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3d714a7-0082-5d4f-ab9a-17597b16c336" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3d714a7-0082-5d4f-ab9a-17597b16c336" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234904} :answer-field/id #uuid "8eddebdf-1405-58bc-9c0f-2eb87f83aa52" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235144} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c56147c9-f2b7-5667-be10-7a59be78f3d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c56147c9-f2b7-5667-be10-7a59be78f3d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234854} :answer-field/id #uuid "d733dbe9-c554-5e94-95f1-066ae833b632" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235234} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd65aedc-568a-52b0-80dd-3058db6f72f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd65aedc-568a-52b0-80dd-3058db6f72f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234893} :answer-field/id #uuid "f602e10d-959a-555e-a86b-ac99268e9349" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235267}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "27a916f2-ae5e-57d0-a97a-ec9cecb80707" :question/math-academy-id "q-138783" :question/problem "$$\nX+Y=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,Z=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices above. Knowing that the matrix representation $T=\\begin{bmatrix}{t}_{11} & {t}_{12} \\\\ {t}_{21} & {t}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$ of a linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=XZ+YZ,\n$$\n\nfind the values ${t}_{ij}.$\n\n${t}_{11}=$ {{field-1}}\n\n${t}_{12}=$ {{field-2}}\n\n${t}_{21}=$ {{field-3}}\n\n${t}_{22}=$ {{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nXZ+YZ=(X+Y)Z.\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =XZ+YZ \\\\  & =(X+Y)Z \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265870 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "306bf8f6-3b52-5e8e-b8bc-cbf0383e7c3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ 8 & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263411} {:answer/id #uuid "458d11a2-6e17-5d80-975f-41aca8028006" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263611} {:answer/id #uuid "d85b3cd4-d405-5203-9c74-8cd0c5576888" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264886} {:answer/id #uuid "e95305ac-6317-500c-b13b-c4fa54f18250" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265028} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a751b3-c8e2-5d94-aaac-e1a351e5be6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8a751b3-c8e2-5d94-aaac-e1a351e5be6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265176} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa1b1ce2-5868-5037-ac84-e98cacb5642f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265550}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "940563cc-cba6-55cd-9e9b-4c5f6961f3e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-130269" :question/problem "Calculate $BA+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nBA+BC=B(A+C).\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+C & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA+BC & =B(A+C) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265880 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19780864-9003-505a-b598-f3378103858e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263242} {:answer/id #uuid "1d6518a0-5e35-59b6-b899-07522f46b179" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -7 & -21 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263268} {:answer/id #uuid "5517ab5e-f687-5ce4-852d-48dfec575a26" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263733} {:answer/id #uuid "55a69114-638a-51d0-954d-1a1fa82cd27a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -8 & 7 \\\\ -3 & 8 & -7 \\\\ -9 & 24 & -21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263735} {:answer/id #uuid "ce129b66-be90-56f8-b1fe-b394c797c064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce129b66-be90-56f8-b1fe-b394c797c064" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264802} :answer-field/id #uuid "42ab1d01-3d95-5a64-a3f9-0807a0efbbe8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265368}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e430effe-7959-580a-be3d-d4b5f50f0d27" :question/math-academy-id "q-130313" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $3$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 & -9 \\\\ -8 & 8 & 24 \\\\ 7 & -7 & -21\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265906 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5721fddb-4ddb-5ceb-8d53-beb5879aabb4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448386} {:answer/id #uuid "94b7a979-8ec2-54e2-90a3-0c1ddb63d731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448387}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94b7a979-8ec2-54e2-90a3-0c1ddb63d731" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448387} :answer-field/id #uuid "808c3874-e879-50ff-9b4f-7080ca2b02ad" :answer-field/key "${A}^{2}B=A(AB)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449233} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f74fb5a-177b-5835-b20e-ce0567027248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448388} {:answer/id #uuid "06d94795-ebf6-5369-a12b-dbfa3c0bde79" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448389}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f74fb5a-177b-5835-b20e-ce0567027248" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448388} :answer-field/id #uuid "7bc69198-ea95-5680-86fb-59feb160bb36" :answer-field/key "$A(B-C)=AB-CA$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449234} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f629e2cf-0d6b-5ebd-ba20-35e8b11008d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448390} {:answer/id #uuid "3ab0f40e-90eb-52f5-8bf5-16588c5aca46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f629e2cf-0d6b-5ebd-ba20-35e8b11008d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448390} :answer-field/id #uuid "ac7d9849-da3b-534a-83ba-7cddee8c3884" :answer-field/key "$B(CA)=(CB)A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449235}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "8250ce52-a1e9-536b-9512-ee968aac3cef" :question/math-academy-id "q-130446" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $4\\times 4$ matrices which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement ${A}^{2}B=A(AB)$ is true. Matrix multiplication is associative and  ${A}^{2}B=AAB=A(AB)$ is always true.\n\n- Statement $A(B-C)=AB-CA$ is false.  Matrix multiplication is distributive and  $A(B-C)=AB-AC.$ However, matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AC\\ne CA$ in general and therefore $A(B-C)\\ne AB-CA$, in general.\n\n- Statement $B(CA)=(CB)A$ is false. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $B(CA)=(BC)A.$ However, matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $BC\\ne CB$ in general and therefore $B(CA)\\ne (CB)A$, in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement  ${A}^{2}B=A(AB)$ is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265907 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "420d6cc9-8195-5ce4-9357-adff9f06e789" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449472} {:answer/id #uuid "dfaff5dd-3001-57cc-a214-27e4b2f13a0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfaff5dd-3001-57cc-a214-27e4b2f13a0b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449473} :answer-field/id #uuid "e83edd0f-1ee5-57a0-b8f2-861740202905" :answer-field/key "$AB=A{I}_{3}B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450690} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8a96d375-e3c1-5d42-b10d-88fedd420645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449474} {:answer/id #uuid "f9d1552b-b0c1-5914-8616-b9aa0f71d996" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8a96d375-e3c1-5d42-b10d-88fedd420645" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449474} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e5d71a8-1832-50ab-a267-82a5ea4c6510" :answer-field/key "$A(B+{I}_{3})=AB$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450691} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fd4a080-8694-528b-99c0-94bb7afe0160" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449476} {:answer/id #uuid "b70ca1e9-55e1-5e83-8b86-ac7385727b87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b70ca1e9-55e1-5e83-8b86-ac7385727b87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449477} :answer-field/id #uuid "43485488-f54f-56dd-98bd-bbf9a37fb3ae" :answer-field/key "${I}_{3}A=A{I}_{3}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450692}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9a216ad8-b070-56d6-a23a-d32e7322b41f" :question/math-academy-id "q-130449" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $3\\times 3$ matrices, and  ${I}_{3}$ is the $3\\times 3$ identity matrix, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement $AB=A{I}_{3}B$ is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $A{I}_{3}B=(A{I}_{3})B=AB.$\n\n- Statement $A(B+{I}_{3})=AB$ is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B+{I}_{3})=AB+A{I}_{3}=AB+A.$ However,  $AB+A\\ne AB,$ in general.\n\n- Statement ${I}_{3}A=A{I}_{3}$ is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  ${I}_{3}A=A{I}_{3}.$\n\nTherefore, only statements $AB=A{I}_{3}B$ and ${I}_{3}A=A{I}_{3}$ are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265909 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e7957644-0d34-5355-b4aa-6843421f4cb6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449478} {:answer/id #uuid "ccfd816a-e282-554a-bc11-458d1326d8d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccfd816a-e282-554a-bc11-458d1326d8d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449479} :answer-field/id #uuid "6fcf8fbd-79c9-5a3f-9c93-3269eb1a6b18" :answer-field/key "$A(BC)=(AB)C$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450693} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5609b0ad-b55f-5942-bbdd-8d585ee962ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449480} {:answer/id #uuid "8db8304a-b1d0-5052-b18c-e9bb08899b11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5609b0ad-b55f-5942-bbdd-8d585ee962ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449480} :answer-field/id #uuid "63b9348d-3f50-5361-9ba1-8262be95c0a0" :answer-field/key "$A(B-C)=AB-CA$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450694} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c5099a79-f035-55b7-a74f-976fa8b79237" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449482} {:answer/id #uuid "96ca6167-ad12-543c-a1c9-e7474101a124" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5099a79-f035-55b7-a74f-976fa8b79237" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449482} :answer-field/id #uuid "fcd08e90-18cc-5f16-8ac5-f89ed5e9b611" :answer-field/key "$CA=AC$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450695}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "da216097-76ab-5a2e-b3ad-662534506edb" :question/math-academy-id "q-130455" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $6\\times 6$ matrices which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement $A(BC)=(AB)C$ is true. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $A(BC)=(AB)C$ is always true.\n\n- Statement $A(B-C)=AB-CA$ is false. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B-C)=AB-AC,$ but $AC\\ne CA$ because matrix multiplication is not commutative in general.\n\n- Statement $CA=AC$  is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $CA\\ne AC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement  $A(BC)=(AB)C$ is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265913 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3e23a78-9cff-5f4f-b321-68256103a287" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449484} {:answer/id #uuid "fc24f783-305e-584a-96dc-56e90c7199d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc24f783-305e-584a-96dc-56e90c7199d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449485} :answer-field/id #uuid "599aa420-34d9-5e48-96d9-1fff3725e551" :answer-field/key "$A{I}_{8}={I}_{8}A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450696} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cd393f3-55f2-599a-aa0a-d18ad1ef34f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449486} {:answer/id #uuid "1566549e-0426-589d-92ea-3d623677f3b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cd393f3-55f2-599a-aa0a-d18ad1ef34f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449486} :answer-field/id #uuid "d184eea5-c9c5-5b93-8586-c6e75fec6d77" :answer-field/key "$AB=BA$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450697} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a7fff099-59fc-5bf2-850f-508b365824eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449488} {:answer/id #uuid "c4b157f5-5880-5d42-b0af-3314832fb23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c4b157f5-5880-5d42-b0af-3314832fb23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449489} :answer-field/id #uuid "c228a2f4-4fa2-5cb5-ad55-1810d368d693" :answer-field/key "$A\\cdot 2{I}_{8}=2A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450698}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c886d4f7-2a2b-5730-a24b-3976b9e31d35" :question/math-academy-id "q-130463" :question/problem "Given that $A$ and $B$  are $8\\times 8$ matrices,  and ${I}_{8}$ is the $8\\times 8$ identity matrix,  which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement $A{I}_{8}={I}_{8}A$ is true. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, however, multiplication by the identity matrix is always commutative. In this case, we have  $A{I}_{8}={I}_{8}A=A.$\n\n- Statement $AB=BA$ is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement $A\\cdot 2{I}_{8}=2A$ is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\cdot 2{I}_{8} & =A({I}_{8}+{I}_{8}) \\\\  & =A{I}_{8}+A{I}_{8} \\\\  & =A+A \\\\  & =2A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, only statements $A{I}_{8}={I}_{8}A$  and $A\\cdot 2{I}_{8}=2A$ are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265914 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f505436-de5e-5e74-9c16-db47f9d3dde8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449490} {:answer/id #uuid "55ad8fd2-983a-52f3-adb4-1610dbb1063d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449491}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f505436-de5e-5e74-9c16-db47f9d3dde8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449490} :answer-field/id #uuid "61886434-6b69-5a05-bc4e-5fe067d4aadb" :answer-field/key "$(CA)B=C(BA)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450699} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20e4cb8a-161c-5b37-8171-e110c0ccabdc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449492} {:answer/id #uuid "c53c0d38-c0d6-534c-98d5-3e8b2cf7c4e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c53c0d38-c0d6-534c-98d5-3e8b2cf7c4e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449493} :answer-field/id #uuid "6517376b-dc67-5612-af55-6316cd92e350" :answer-field/key "$(A+A)B=2AB$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "45243252-dbf8-5dba-81eb-702f3231cb73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449494} {:answer/id #uuid "5489dffc-c13b-505b-b7ba-aa63f4669cd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449495}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45243252-dbf8-5dba-81eb-702f3231cb73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449494} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd0867ba-7318-50a7-adfb-0f8ddb112341" :answer-field/key "$CB=BC$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186450701}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "ca328f5c-fde3-5a0e-88ed-9bc8ff6b0334" :question/math-academy-id "q-130478" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $7\\times 7$ matrices which of the following statements are always true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement $(CA)B=C(BA)$  is false. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $(CA)B=C(AB)$ is always true. However,  matrix multiplication is not commutative,   $AB\\ne BA$ in general. Therefore, $(CA)B\\ne C(BA)$ in general.\n\n- Statement $(A+A)B=2AB$ is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $(A+A)B=AB+AB=2AB$ is always true.\n\n- Statement $CB=BC$ is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative in general, so $CB\\ne BC$ in general.\n\nTherefore, only statement $(A+A)B=2AB$ is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292858 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "274faa62-4b23-54e2-ac7e-f2924e7c23d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "274faa62-4b23-54e2-ac7e-f2924e7c23d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290794} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cb19be5-4f4f-5fa0-a4c4-7913e344efe3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292124} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93e87f28-94c9-5988-b696-19c20bdb9dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93e87f28-94c9-5988-b696-19c20bdb9dab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291270} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0da4143-5297-5b70-86e3-2956d34435fa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292283} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb645714-2a42-5a0a-8871-a4b6b95039fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb645714-2a42-5a0a-8871-a4b6b95039fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291698} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3bf1c8f-05e1-534c-a5f6-a9092084607f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292289}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "ebd8942f-54d2-577f-b680-a6f2a8658e9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-275515" :question/problem "Calculate $AB+AC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n|  |  | $4$ | $3$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB+AC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} | $0$ | $-2$ |  |\n|  |  | $-1$ | {{field-3}} | $5$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law \n\n$$\nAB+AC=A(B+C).\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $B+C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B+C & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB+AC & =A(B+C) \\\\  & =A{I}_{3} \\\\  & =A \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292859 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b078db42-ad93-5fd2-9dbb-b3b4553a9c0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b078db42-ad93-5fd2-9dbb-b3b4553a9c0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291398} :answer-field/id #uuid "02615eb4-e49b-59d7-b652-4ca3a6d8d8db" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291740} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bd2967e-32d5-57d9-a3b8-75b2b7e7147f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bd2967e-32d5-57d9-a3b8-75b2b7e7147f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291157} :answer-field/id #uuid "76e5432f-a801-5d71-bc07-6eb03bc28ed4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292106} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b36c894c-59ef-574f-abe9-591a4458eb02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291413}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b36c894c-59ef-574f-abe9-591a4458eb02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291413} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1b2699f-628c-53c3-abce-26c84635cb5c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292331}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "973f3f2c-d8ff-5109-9a91-e7eb0086d029" :question/math-academy-id "q-275518" :question/problem "Find $AC+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -6 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{5} & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3} & 4 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n|  |  | $8\\sqrt{5}$ | $-4$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AC+BC=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | {{field-2}} | $16$ |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | $12$ | $20$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAC+BC=(A+B)C.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+B$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+B & =\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 6 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & -6 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =4{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC+BC & =(A+B)C \\\\  & =4{I}_{3}C \\\\  & =4C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8\\sqrt{5} & -4 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 4\\sqrt{3} & 16 \\\\ -8 & 12 & 20\\text{ }\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292860 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "62b9489d-1bd9-53ad-9584-412222a7fecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "62b9489d-1bd9-53ad-9584-412222a7fecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291053} :answer-field/id #