-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ace3f9bd-8053-505b-92e3-d7127e869294" :question/math-academy-id "q-275521" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n| $ABC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $2\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-11 & 11 \\\\ -8 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299802 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c6d5cde5-f8df-5fc9-a0e0-c09bfdb02cd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298421}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c6d5cde5-f8df-5fc9-a0e0-c09bfdb02cd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298421} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccab8471-735f-5ae8-b673-5e8ed001726e" :answer-field/key 