 $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=XZ-YZ,\n$$\n\nfind the values ${t}_{ij}.$\n\n${t}_{11}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,{t}_{12}=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${t}_{21}=$\n{{field-3}}\n$\\,{t}_{22}=$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nXZ-YZ=(X-Y)Z.\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =XZ-YZ \\\\  & =(X-Y)Z \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 9 \\\\ -1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186613779 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49566a5a-3ff9-5be8-83b2-2bdded8a30d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613392}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49566a5a-3ff9-5be8-83b2-2bdded8a30d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613392} :answer-field/id #uuid "769c6d5c-0d7a-52e1-9473-a23b7563ec4d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613676} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8b03074e-9616-57a8-91f0-3ca96adc9fc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b03074e-9616-57a8-91f0-3ca96adc9fc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613477} :answer-field/id #uuid "aed8083b-0775-5107-aefc-2ae24d5278c9" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613693} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c3204d2-3d6f-5260-94b9-1fc7896c9818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c3204d2-3d6f-5260-94b9-1fc7896c9818" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613451} :answer-field/id #uuid "daa49209-96b5-527a-ba4b-cb78448aaf5b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613715} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6614a417-d4ae-56a7-8f86-b8c0ab4febe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6614a417-d4ae-56a7-8f86-b8c0ab4febe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613437} :answer-field/id #uuid "f59a281d-f7d1-5cd2-bd0d-1d66d1773704" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186613728}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8319fedc-5753-50f8-9061-f1f4303f25f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-137872" :question/problem "$$\nX+Y=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\,Z=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -4 \\\\ -10 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices above. Knowing that the matrix representation $T=\\begin{bmatrix}{t}_{11} & {t}_{12} \\\\ {t}_{21} & {t}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$ of a linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=XZ+YZ,\n$$\n\nfind the values ${t}_{ij}.$\n\n${t}_{11}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\,{t}_{12}=$\n{{field-2}}\n\n${t}_{21}=$\n{{field-3}}\n$\\,{t}_{22}=$\n{{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nXZ+YZ=(X+Y)Z.\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =XZ+YZ \\\\  & =(X+Y)Z \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -4 \\\\ -10 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ -7 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186629270 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd39dfca-2e0b-5d0c-99b4-fb6bbddff83d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629053}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd39dfca-2e0b-5d0c-99b4-fb6bbddff83d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629053} :answer-field/id #uuid "159cdec6-a2f0-5547-8cf7-8a0b345160aa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629141} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "df157b4e-4bd5-5afe-bfc1-9c8b63d323f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df157b4e-4bd5-5afe-bfc1-9c8b63d323f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-68" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629083} :answer-field/id #uuid "23204e02-a85b-5138-ae6e-4b72698ed92c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629150} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25844569-f541-5d94-90cf-57abbfbaa16e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628774}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25844569-f541-5d94-90cf-57abbfbaa16e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "34" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628774} :answer-field/id #uuid "3bc9200a-6293-532f-8d4a-a84939731b12" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2477118f-5d40-5b7c-b0ad-0ab680cefec4" :question/math-academy-id "q-320020" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$ABC=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-3}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 3$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $1\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding only $1$ entry, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 3$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}(-1)\\cdot 2+5\\cdot (-3)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-17\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $(AB)$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)\\,C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-17\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-68 & 0 & 34\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186629276 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "258f302a-bd8f-584f-a29d-db45c779e0e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628775}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "258f302a-bd8f-584f-a29d-db45c779e0e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-19" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628775} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e4e99c5-75ea-5628-bd88-5be4e4eb7eae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629155} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81117680-9f10-5c23-913a-b317c45f1fe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "81117680-9f10-5c23-913a-b317c45f1fe2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628927} :answer-field/id #uuid "fbb99a80-64ea-514f-a9e8-6d1c466aee9d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629249}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "2ea71558-54ec-572a-9d1d-713eb9802e6e" :question/math-academy-id "q-320025" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"35px\" rowspan=\"2\">$ABC=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, and $C$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $1\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $2$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $2\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $4$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-19 & 32\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186629288 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "242e8c6c-5ef6-5530-b221-67b1724cb924" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628771} {:answer/id #uuid "467beaa2-f789-5f60-9ede-95bff4fd79a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628834} {:answer/id #uuid "63fa0419-3548-5eb3-a74f-0c8ec26478d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628877} {:answer/id #uuid "83287c90-7f72-5277-9910-eef08a8e9f0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628929} {:answer/id #uuid "c84f9faa-27b0-5feb-b898-8ee328b2817d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629046}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63fa0419-3548-5eb3-a74f-0c8ec26478d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628877} :answer-field/id #uuid "ead74683-8b8c-5101-b102-d3a41b2c166a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "4f54e4e8-85c8-5be4-a909-f55503250f4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-75661" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $4\\times 4$ matrices, which of the following statements are always true?\n\nI. $A(B-C)=AB-AC$\n\nII. $AB=BA$\n\nIII. $(AC)B=A(CB)$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so \n\n$$\nA(B-C)=A(B+(-C))=AB+A(-C)=AB-AC.\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $AB\\ne BA$ in general.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is associative, so $(AC)B=A(CB)$  in general.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186629328 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b1a2fe9-8acf-5209-842f-457138328f72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628887} {:answer/id #uuid "8c1e400d-a09e-534a-8be6-6acd27c855a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628943} {:answer/id #uuid "d3b88920-7f6b-5e51-888f-cac24d60b9f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629057} {:answer/id #uuid "dc8ff2a5-5409-58c7-acbc-0f1147fc82a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629080} {:answer/id #uuid "f4a24263-6bb0-5a83-870a-7f39ca73dc7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3b88920-7f6b-5e51-888f-cac24d60b9f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629057} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb48ebea-5c12-5e74-899a-177996703a8f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629242}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "b81a7dc6-23a0-5a37-be19-b0f5da8ca9f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-130453" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $5\\times 5$ matrices which of the following statements are always true? \n\nI. $A(B-C)=A(C-B)$\n\nII. $A(CB)=(AC)B$\n\nIII. $A{B}^{2}=(AB)B$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false.  Matrix multiplication is distributive, so   $A(B-C)=AB-AC$ and $A(C-B)=AC-BC.$ However,  $AB-AC\\ne AC-AB,$ in general. Therefore $A(B-C)\\ne A(C-B)$, in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $A(CB)=(AC)B$ is always true.\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $A{B}^{2}=A(BB)=(AB)B$ is always true.\n\nTherefore, only statements II and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186629329 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "171a931e-aa04-55a2-9b28-d2a04fa7aa2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628743} {:answer/id #uuid "20b3cab3-4542-5819-9cb5-a89999e8e2b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628760} {:answer/id #uuid "8cc81170-862e-596c-8360-8088ce74703d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628945} {:answer/id #uuid "b88450ba-c795-50bd-9557-1eb37f71f7a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629017} {:answer/id #uuid "d499a780-bd64-57b9-9d55-d65085448926" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629060}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d499a780-bd64-57b9-9d55-d65085448926" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629060} :answer-field/id #uuid "35dfb0dc-3fc5-50e8-b885-b8e8e3bdf2f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629160}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "baa88cfe-429c-543d-bba8-a1f699b6bda3" :question/math-academy-id "q-75718" :question/problem "Given that $A,B,$ and $C$ are $6\\times 6$ matrices which of the following statements are always true? \n\nI. $BCB=B(BC)$\n\nII. $A(B-C)=AB-AC$\n\nIII. $C(BA)=(CB)A$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider the statements one by one.\n\n- Statement I is false.  Matrix multiplication is associative and  $BCB=B(CB).$ However, matrix multiplication is not commutative, so $CB\\ne BC$ in general and therefore $BCB\\ne B(BC)$, in general.\n\n- Statement II is true. Matrix multiplication is distributive, so $A(B-C)=AB-AC.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Matrix multiplication is associative and  $C(BA)=(CB)A$ is always true.\n\nTherefore, only statements  II and III are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186629333 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59ac3224-816e-5a7c-8d96-c4c0b571c2a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628857} {:answer/id #uuid "6f00fa10-59de-5bff-9c89-56a716168fe3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628895} {:answer/id #uuid "b30c07fb-0360-5d0c-9e6c-6d002ba83421" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629007} {:answer/id #uuid "c53305e8-8bb3-5a3a-8888-0bf672824757" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629040} {:answer/id #uuid "fd1d6be5-80c0-561f-b9ee-b0247aad9bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd1d6be5-80c0-561f-b9ee-b0247aad9bd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629128} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8ca504d-9cd7-5c42-98a8-c6b513b5e39a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629227}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c6eccfba-8d60-5003-9d46-d8b008d34466" :question/math-academy-id "q-75652" :question/problem "Calculate $CB-CA$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{3} & -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{3} & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law \n\n$$\nCB-CA=C(B-A).\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $B-A$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B-A & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3 & 3 & -4 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{3} & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{3} & -3 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CB-CA & =C(B-A) \\\\  & =C\\cdot (-1){I}_{3} \\\\  & =-C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186629343 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49ca1606-56dc-55c2-8578-2acdf2df4897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & 12 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 2 \\\\ -7 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628840} {:answer/id #uuid "63fd9207-b3f3-5221-9412-2055039607f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628878} {:answer/id #uuid "9169b9a8-19ad-5f2a-9986-7fc4bf27a992" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -10 & 2 \\\\ -14 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628952} {:answer/id #uuid "df44b9ab-ef97-5100-949d-fb74baa256aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -10 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629084} {:answer/id #uuid "f0476b4a-24b5-5c1a-8a67-8ab2d8e22136" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629107}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9169b9a8-19ad-5f2a-9986-7fc4bf27a992" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -10 & 2 \\\\ -14 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186628952} :answer-field/id #uuid "905a2bda-b4cb-5f0c-998a-55ab2afc9a43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186629194}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e2956fb8-8468-580b-b6a5-e7a3c2e541b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-130281" :question/problem "Find $AB+CB$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -6 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAB+CB=(A+C)B.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+C & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -6 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 7\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =2{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB+CB & =(A+C)B \\\\  & =2{I}_{3}B \\\\  & =2B \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -10 & 2 \\\\ -14 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186649824 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4313732b-563a-55dc-8ca7-78581cd77a15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-35 & 25 \\\\ 42 & -18 \\\\ -5 & 21\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649380} {:answer/id #uuid "47390465-ab03-59b6-ad5e-9cf8cffc4593" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}28 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 35\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649388} {:answer/id #uuid "57c7e7f4-9b6f-578d-a160-643cba921eff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-15 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649425} {:answer/id #uuid "8ee3d17b-7676-5413-b495-384c53b0bc12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 & -12 \\\\ 35 & -28 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649524} {:answer/id #uuid "cdf21d84-a23e-5c34-9fca-ebad21063f40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 35 \\\\ 28 & -12 \\\\ -15 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ee3d17b-7676-5413-b495-384c53b0bc12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}15 & -12 \\\\ 35 & -28 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649524} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f51278f-ee43-5032-a5a8-e7f0378d75e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649754}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "31687a2b-cc68-5ba3-a320-59a64870dd5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-42003" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $3$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}5 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}15 & -12 \\\\ 35 & -28 \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186649832 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "afa897e3-bec4-5f88-93d5-7db1ac1ca0f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ -8 & 12 \\\\ 18 & -27\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649584} {:answer/id #uuid "afb3c867-7599-5ee2-b2e8-39d64dd1816e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 18\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649585} {:answer/id #uuid "e1e716c2-b879-5dd2-a6f7-d656cfce4a61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -8 & 18\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649663} {:answer/id #uuid "eae1bce1-1b37-56cd-872c-571598d1a2e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 \\\\ -16 & 24 \\\\ 36 & -54\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649679} {:answer/id #uuid "fa5167ed-3b6b-5d91-8525-04f6c3b12108" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 8 \\\\ 9 & -9\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649704}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eae1bce1-1b37-56cd-872c-571598d1a2e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 \\\\ -16 & 24 \\\\ 36 & -54\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649679} :answer-field/id #uuid "7372f355-a8ea-5930-a427-d4650afe8524" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649756}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "3f365320-c37a-5260-b123-1955c90d35a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-130309" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix, $B$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix, and $C$ is a $1\\times 2$ matrix. Therefore, \n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$, we will obtain a $3\\times 1$ matrix, which will require finding $3$ entries, while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$, we will obtain a $3\\times 2$ matrix, which will require finding $6$ entries.\n\nSo, we find the product $AB$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $AB$ by $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =(AB)C \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 6 \\\\ -16 & 24 \\\\ 36 & -54\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186649880 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98db1f97-05ad-542a-834e-da8739b3ac75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "98db1f97-05ad-542a-834e-da8739b3ac75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649548} :answer-field/id #uuid "11b2c8a7-0e02-5c0b-99c8-104567b9da48" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649725} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bafbf1b8-66aa-567f-98b2-420dd24a5775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649603}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bafbf1b8-66aa-567f-98b2-420dd24a5775" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649603} :answer-field/id #uuid "29db3a45-608f-5486-aec0-b0a0ae7240a5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649735} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3d70b6a-4494-57e3-91a0-dd689e1bba4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3d70b6a-4494-57e3-91a0-dd689e1bba4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649693} :answer-field/id #uuid "92eb4cb5-20c3-548a-8db9-09e31c9738ed" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186649770}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "ccf609af-63ab-558e-b2d1-560aae618250" :question/math-academy-id "q-320019" :question/problem "Calculate $ABC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $ABC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the associative law\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nNotice that $A$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix, $B$ is a $2\\times 3$ matrix, and $C$ is a $3\\times 1$ matrix. Therefore,\n\n- multiplying $A$ by $B$ produces a $3\\times 3$ matrix (nine entries to compute), while\n\n- multiplying $B$ by $C$ produces a $2\\times 1$ matrix (two entries to compute).\n\nSo, we find the product $BC$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2\\cdot 1+0\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\ (-3)\\cdot 1+1\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply $A$ by $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC & =A(BC) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1\\cdot 0+(-4)\\cdot 4 \\\\ 3\\cdot 0+2\\cdot 4 \\\\ (-2)\\cdot 0+5\\cdot 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-16 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 20\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717470 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "890fa9d6-3c92-5afd-9b8a-13b62013ff65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "890fa9d6-3c92-5afd-9b8a-13b62013ff65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3} + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717478} :answer-field/id #uuid "4820a725-21b2-5d95-96e1-7de046824b72" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717472} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12af1456-65c9-522d-8c08-9f6cbed24092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 - \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12af1456-65c9-522d-8c08-9f6cbed24092" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 - \\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717465} :answer-field/id #uuid "783e3bec-8a3a-56f4-8c44-24f0086d977e" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717477} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47364c7e-522f-5c11-859d-f8f9013868f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47364c7e-522f-5c11-859d-f8f9013868f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 + \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717471} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc4ff29e-79ca-509c-9c19-f5918bb6cc9e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717482} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "624aab4e-da47-552f-ab68-0d9e8b08266b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "624aab4e-da47-552f-ab68-0d9e8b08266b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1 - \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717475} :answer-field/id #uuid "e89ce330-74dd-5d98-b36c-3353f17cc87c" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717485}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "4439cfd8-ddb4-5d6b-abbb-4358d8314163" :question/problem "Calculate $AC-BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & - \\sqrt{3} & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe table gives the entries of $AC-BC$. Fill in the missing entries.\n\n| Row | Column 1 | Column 2 | Column 3 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | $2$ |\n| 2 | $-3$ | {{field-3}} | $\\sqrt{5}$ |\n| 3 | $\\sqrt{2} + 2$ | $-1$ | {{field-4}} |\n" :question/worked-solution "Factor out the shared right factor $C$ without moving it to the left:\n\n$$\nAC-BC=(A-B)C.\n$$\n\nSubtract corresponding entries first:\n\n$$\nA-B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThe result is not a scalar multiple of the identity. Multiply each row of $A-B$ by each column of $C$. The three output rows are, respectively, row 1 plus row 2 of $C$, row 3 minus row 2 of $C$, and row 1 minus row 3 of $C$. For the missing entries:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} (AC-BC)_{11}&=1\\cdot\\sqrt{2}+1\\cdot1+0\\cdot(-2)=\\sqrt{2}+1, \\\\ (AC-BC)_{12}&=1\\cdot1+1\\cdot(-\\sqrt{3})+0\\cdot2=1-\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ (AC-BC)_{22}&=0\\cdot1+(-1)(-\\sqrt{3})+1\\cdot2=\\sqrt{3}+2, \\\\ (AC-BC)_{33}&=1\\cdot2+0\\cdot0+(-1)\\sqrt{5}=2-\\sqrt{5}. \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the complete matrix is\n\n$$\nAC-BC=\\begin{bmatrix}1 + \\sqrt{2} & 1 - \\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ -3 & \\sqrt{3} + 2 & \\sqrt{5} \\\\ \\sqrt{2} + 2 & -1 & 2 - \\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717483 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32727c35-b087-587e-95bc-c023683ef155" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32727c35-b087-587e-95bc-c023683ef155" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717468} :answer-field/id #uuid "2dc9e755-aee5-5c9e-8286-58e87897f1cf" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717467} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "064944f6-2ec9-52fe-b862-887092780e91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717464}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "064944f6-2ec9-52fe-b862-887092780e91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2 \\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717464} :answer-field/id #uuid "54c52198-f06e-52a3-a631-1b61a1187358" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717473} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c2de559-ec55-547f-a156-36e05b276aa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c2de559-ec55-547f-a156-36e05b276aa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 2 \\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717481} :answer-field/id #uuid "f700a76f-88b5-58d0-ac17-1fad462d5d33" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "d0572715-7415-58c8-af0e-c23c5eaeab1b" :question/problem "Calculate $CB-CA$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & - \\sqrt{3} \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe table gives the entries of $CB-CA$. Fill in the missing entries.\n\n| Row | Column 1 | Column 2 | Column 3 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | {{field-1}} | $2$ | $0$ |\n| 2 | $-4$ | $0$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | {{field-3}} | $-6$ | $-2$ |\n" :question/worked-solution "Both products have the shared left factor $C$. Keep the subtraction in the order $B-A$:\n\n$$\nCB-CA=C(B-A).\n$$\n\nSubtract corresponding entries of $A$ from $B$. Each diagonal difference is $-2$ and each off-diagonal difference is $0$:\n\n$$\nB-A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}=-2I_3.\n$$\n\nTherefore multiply every entry of $C$ by $-2$:\n\n$$\nCB-CA=C(-2I_3)=-2C=\\begin{bmatrix}- 2 \\sqrt{2} & 2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 0 & 2 \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 2 & -6 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nIn particular, the missing entries are $-2\\sqrt{2}$, $2\\sqrt{3}$, and $2$, in row order."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717484 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1808d49c-c9c9-5838-80ca-0c0d61264ec5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717466} {:answer/id #uuid "40c85861-9ed3-5600-9757-157d1b8fd6dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717469} {:answer/id #uuid "5c0a1080-7e20-5999-9519-3b08614e54b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717474} {:answer/id #uuid "667b2e8a-cee8-5486-a027-8feac086aa8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 8 & -4 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717476} {:answer/id #uuid "9a034b15-8215-5bd6-a13a-7a50ea6dd9db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "40c85861-9ed3-5600-9757-157d1b8fd6dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717469} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b8ecaff-be96-5094-ba3c-8c3956197c1c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717479}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e27ab8e5-06c4-561d-8fca-53ea44b21aa8" :question/problem "Calculate $AB+AC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nChoose the resulting matrix." :question/worked-solution "Factor out the shared left factor $A$, keeping it on the left:\n\n$$\nAB+AC=A(B+C).\n$$\n\nAdd corresponding entries of $B$ and $C$. The diagonal entries each sum to $1$ and all other entries sum to $0$:\n\n$$\nB+C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}=I_3.\n$$\n\nMultiplication by the identity leaves a matrix unchanged:\n\n$$\nAB+AC=AI_3=A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717497 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "695ee893-2e8d-5508-8a3f-417e7a79dc72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "695ee893-2e8d-5508-8a3f-417e7a79dc72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717500} :answer-field/id #uuid "07249a84-8cc4-5146-be2c-a5fcd4b990c4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717487} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a012feeb-d45c-5634-ae4