The associative law changes the grouping while preserving factor order:\n\n$$\nABC=(AB)C=A(BC).\n$$\n\nAll three factors are $3\\times3$, so intermediate dimensions do not distinguish the groupings. Computing $BC$ exposes cancellation. For example, the first entry is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(BC)_{1,1} &=(3)\\cdot(1)+(2)\\cdot(-1)+(-1)\\cdot(0) \\\\ &=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe complete product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC &=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe diagonal intermediate multiplies the columns of $A$. Now complete the product. For example, the first entry is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(ABC)_{1,1} &=(3)\\cdot(1)+(3)\\cdot(0)+(3)\\cdot(0) \\\\ &=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe complete product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}ABC &=A(BC) \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ &=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186717942 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8c74e5d-9168-57fa-ac96-4f168416d337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a8c74e5d-9168-57fa-ac96-4f168416d337" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717925} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c31acbf-b363-5848-a323-899fab30d5a9" :answer-field/key "field-7" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186717879} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b0e30e3-60c4-5d45-bef9-e9484065a6ad" :answer/type {:db/id #e