\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThen the left side is $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and the proposed right side is $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$, so this is a counterexample.\n\n- $C(BA)=(CA)B$ is **not always true**. Associativity moves parentheses while retaining the order of every factor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C(BA) &=(CB)A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe proposed right side is not guaranteed to equal this result. For example, take\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThen the left side is $\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and the proposed right side is $\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$, so this is a counterexample.\n\nSelect $I_2A=A$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718038 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fa4da2e-91cb-52fa-8bac-ad7ee2c4d0ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718034} {:answer/id #uuid "94334769-4014-5bbf-960b-8119c23bdd8f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718047}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2fa4da2e-91cb-52fa-8bac-ad7ee2c4d0ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718034} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b01f883-c8d9-5bc6-8e21-94c91994edf3" :answer-field/key "$C(AB)=(CA)B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718045} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "722df149-01b1-5e96-9bf7-ae9d1321f2e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718042} {:answer/id #uuid "f53b1c44-0c7f-54ed-9625-e154496bbb00" :answer