ppears; the arbitrary matrix remains.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CI_2 &=C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe proposed right side is not guaranteed to equal this result. For example, take\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\quad C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThen the left side is $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and the proposed right side is $\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$, so this is a counterexample.\n\n- $C(AB)=(CA)B$ is **always true**. Associativity moves parentheses while retaining the order of every factor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C(AB) &=(CA)B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSelect $B(C+A)=BC+BA$, $C(AB)=(CA)B$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718040 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b2bb884-5c03-503c-8d5e-b416c654da1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718030} {:answer/id #uuid "eef72ee3-13d2-5041-9cf5-b3053d0d8b3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718059}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b2bb884-5c03-503c-8d5e-b416c654da1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718030} :answer-field/id #uuid "05b51ad9-438d-585c-bd42-19189199ee95" :answer-field/key "$BI_2=B$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718025} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f11542d-5bfc-53a0-b45e-380e8f15f801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718031} {:answer/id #uuid "4fc3d147-330e-5871-8869-192e5638a6d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 175921867