always true**. Associativity moves parentheses while retaining the order of every factor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C(BA) &=(CB)A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe proposed right side is not guaranteed to equal this result. For example, take\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThen the left side is $\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and the proposed right side is $\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$, so this is a counterexample.\n\nSelect $BI_2=B$, $(B+C)A=BA+CA$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186718049 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14c7e79a-efc8-5546-9b21-86b10f92b6b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718026} {:answer/id #uuid "9ecab358-4026-5ae1-b519-068d715cb220" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14c7e79a-efc8-5546-9b21-86b10f92b6b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718026} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b81b81d-e3df-5081-8236-fe57c7592b2a" :answer-field/key "$B(AC)=(BA)C$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718036} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "95758370-76ec-5c80-bc78-a5682fbae46f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718048} {:answer/id #uuid "d4cb8ac6-236c-59fe-89a3-2bac45965cf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718057}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "95758370-76ec-5c80-bc78-a5682fbae46f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718048} :answer-field/id #uuid "8659799e-0d97-555e-a24c-7309d70d19fe" :answer-field/key "$AI_2=A$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718044} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28221c1c-3df7-561f-b81e-27552137499b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718032} {:answer/id #uuid "5f0a43b8-c7a0-56ca-ab2b-864160402ad3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f0a43b8-c7a0-56ca-ab2b-864160402ad3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718041} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3e478cc-aedf-56ff-ab98-89761c4163a8" :answer-field/key "$(C+A)B=CB+BA$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186718054}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "994bf2d3-1f8f-54d2-96ad-147049cddadc" :question/problem "Let $A$, $B$, and $C$ be $2\\times 2$ real matrices, and let $I_2$ be the identity matrix.\n\nRemember: regrouping a product changes its parentheses without changing the order of its factors.\n\nWhich statements are always true? Select all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- $(C+A)B=CB+BA$ is **not always true**. Distribute with the outside factor on the same side in each product.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(C+A)B &=CB+AB\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe proposed right side is not guaranteed to equal this result. For example, take\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad B=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\quad C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nThen the left side is $\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and the proposed right side is $\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$, so this is a counterexample.\n\n- $AI_2=A$ is **always true**. The identity factor disappears; the arbitrary matrix remains.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AI_2 &=A\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- $B(AC)=(BA)C$ is **always true**. Associativity moves parentheses while retaining the order of every factor.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(AC) &=(BA)C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSelect $AI_2=A$, $B(AC)=(BA)C$."}]}
